meta {
  name: List streams with no group
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{groupService}}/streams
  body: none
  auth: none
}

tests {
  test("refuses a listing for no group", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(400);
  });
}

docs {
  # List streams with no group

  The same index with no group key, which is refused.

  A stream lives in a group: the relay carries a path under a group's prefix and nothing else, so a caller naming no key is asking about streams nobody holds.
  What clears the refusal is a group key, which `List group streams` sends.
}
